const rows=[
["M001",9,"Division-ring scalars, additive commutative group/module, Fintype index, FiniteDimensional, linear independence and cardinality=finrank are all present in the restatement. The exact conclusion is span(range f)=top. The primed declaration imposes no Nonempty index condition; the neighboring unprimed declaration does. No condition was dropped.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/FiniteDimensional/Lemmas.lean:253-271"],
["M002",10,"The restatement retains CommSemiring R₀, AddCommMonoid A, Module R₀ A, Semiring S₀ and Algebra R₀ S₀, with an arbitrary indexed basis. The theorem identifies baseChange's ith vector as 1⊗B_i. The extra construction sentence faithfully unfolds the source definition (singleton tensor basis reindexed by punitProd); it is not a claim that a library definition alone is a new theorem.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/TensorProduct/Basis.lean:29-75"],
["M003",11,"The semiring, additive commutative monoid/module, strong rank condition, finite index and supplied basis exactly match the full native telescope and finrank=card conclusion. The prose definition of strong rank condition agrees with its native class; there is no additional assumed module freeness or nontriviality beyond these stated premises.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/StrongRankCondition.lean:450-454","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/InvariantBasisNumber.lean:116-123"],
["M004",12,"The finite-product finrank formula retains the semiring strong rank condition, Fintype index, and each component's AddCommMonoid, Module, Free and Finite premises. The source explicitly needs freeness, and the candidate includes it. Cached stdout is marked M001; metadata_reuse.original_source_id=M001 explicitly maps it to current sources.M004. Declaration, complete signature, module, commit and source digest agree under that mapping; it is disclosed reuse, not a fresh probe.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/Constructions.lean:269-302"],
["M005",13,"The source is the same-ring linear-equivalence theorem, over a semiring and additive commutative monoid modules, with no finite-dimensionality or rank-condition premise. The restatement includes exactly those structures and linear equivalence and preserves the finrank equality, without converting it into an unstated dimension theorem.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/Finrank.lean:38-43","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/Finrank.lean:113-118"],
["M006",14,"The source quantifies natural n,p and assumes Prime p; its iff is p∣n! ↔ p≤n. The candidate's u,ℓ renaming preserves the natural-number domain, primality, both directions and the n=0 endpoint.","Mathlib/Data/Nat/Prime/Factorial.lean:21-29"],
["M007",15,"The source requires nonzero natural n and a natural p≠1, with existential natural e,n′, p∤n′ and n=p^e*n′. The restatement faithfully keeps those conditions and existential quantifiers; it does not strengthen the source to require prime p or claim a rational valuation without the separate local bridge.","Mathlib/Data/Nat/Factorization/Basic.lean:273-279"],
["M008",16,"DivisionRing F, AddCommGroup A, Module F A and finite subset B are all retained. The conclusion concerns the submodule span_F B, not the whole ambient A. This is exactly FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite and its native context.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/FiniteDimensional/Defs.lean:190-201"],
["M009",17,"The official declaration is a proposition-valued instance implemented as a kernel theorem: every module over a division ring (with AddCommGroup and Module structures) is free. Those are the complete native premises and agree with the restatement; source lines construct an actual basis. This does not assume finite dimension or freeness of a general R-submodule of ℂ.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Basis/VectorSpace.lean:38-43","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Basis/VectorSpace.lean:143-155"],
["M010",18,"The official shortcut is a proposition-valued instance/kernel theorem requiring CommRing R₀ and Nontrivial R₀. Both appear in the candidate. The stated finite-free injectivity condition is exactly the StrongRankCondition class definition, with source and target dimensions in the correct direction.","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/FreeModule/StrongRankCondition.lean:13-27","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/FreeModule/StrongRankCondition.lean:39-42","Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/InvariantBasisNumber.lean:116-123"]
];
